    <summary>Audit CI/CD pipeline authority: GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI and Bitbucket Pipelines</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
taudit builds an authority graph from your CI/CD pipeline YAML — who can run what, with which secrets and tokens, from which trigger — and reports where untrusted input, over-scoped identities, or self-mutating steps give a pull request more power than it should have. It parses GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI and Bitbucket Pipelines, gates merges with a policy file (`taudit verify`), and emits terminal, JSON, SARIF and CloudEvents output with stable finding fingerprints for baselines and suppressions.

This package installs the `taudit` CLI (x86_64 Windows), downloaded from the GitHub Release for tag `v1.3.3` and verified by SHA-256 at install time. Nothing is bundled in the package itself.

The binary is not code-signed. Release notes and checksums: https://github.com/0ryant/taudit/releases/tag/v1.3.3 — user guide: https://github.com/0ryant/taudit/blob/main/USERGUIDE.md
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/0ryant/taudit/releases/tag/v1.3.3</releaseNotes>
